{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476426431,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgyMzU0MDM0Mg=="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476426431,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDgyMzU0MDM0Mw=="},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1476433724,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MzczOTk4Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1007#issuecomment-253739987"},"message":"To have the behaviour of `git -C src/raw fetch --all`, you'd need `datalad update -d src/raw --fetch-all`.\nDon't know atm, whether it actually expected a master branch or just tried, but `--all` isn't default behaviour (as it isn't for `git fetch`).\n\nRegarding telling what to update rather than where to update from:\nIt simply follows `git fetch` atm and this totally makes sense to me ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476434087,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1Mzc0MTEzMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1007#issuecomment-253741130"},"message":"\u003e To have the behaviour of git -C src/raw fetch --all, you'd need datalad update -d src/raw --fetch-all.\n\u003e Don't know atm, whether it actually expected a master branch or just tried, but --all isn't default behaviour (as it isn't for git fetch).\n\nThat is fine with me but `git fetch` does this:\n\n```\n% git -C src/raw fetch\n-\u003e exit 0\n```\n\nwhile `update` results in a fatal error.\n\n\u003e Regarding telling what to update rather than where to update from:\n\u003e It simply follows git fetch atm and this totally makes sense to me ;-)\n\nWe know that this is no argument. Imagine I would say: \"`install` follows `git clone` and this totally makes sense to me\" :-(","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1476444131,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1Mzc3NDI1Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1007#issuecomment-253774252"},"message":"I agree, the fatal error isn't desirable and I don't say this isn't buggy.\n\n\u003e We know that this is no argument. Imagine I would say: \"install follows git clone and this totally makes sense to me\" :-(\n\nOkay. So, the argument is: `update` operates on a dataset. This is derived from CWD or `-d` as everywhere else. So the only thing left would be the remote to update from. Otherwise we suddenly start to specify the dataset to operate on by NOT using `-d`, which to me seems to be an inconsistent API. Of course we can do it, but then you have to specify the dataset in different ways depending on what command you use. Doesn't sound reasonable to me.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1476444546,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1Mzc3NTM2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1007#issuecomment-253775363"},"message":"I agree, but it is in conflict with the desired behavior of `install` and `get` as per most recent API eruption. One of the themes there was auto-guessing what dataset to operate on (e.g. `get path2 path2`, where both paths do not share a dataset).\n\nOnly trying to figure out a way to be able to describe how the API is meant to be -- I had hoped to be able to write it down one day, but it seems I am not the chosen one ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1476466450,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1Mzg2ODc0OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1007#issuecomment-253868749"},"message":"\u003e Only trying to figure out a way to be able to describe how the API is meant to be -- I had hoped to\n\u003e be able to write it down one day, but it seems I am not the chosen one ;-)\n\nYou are the chosen one, even though they nail you to the crest and throw stones at you!  So please don't feel stopped.  Just remember that we had already some write ups on how API was \"meant to be\" (original grant, numerous google docs and github PRs/issues), so it would be nice for it to reflect accumulated experience, and if anything to address known issues.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487262277,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDM4MDA4Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1007#issuecomment-280380083"},"message":"The chosen one say: This is no open issue.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487262277,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTY1MjcwNTU0"},"status":2}]}